# Print command help for `z4x source` (`-z4x-cmd-source`).

eval "$_z4x_opt"

print -Pr -- "$(<<\END
%F{4}Usage:%f %F{2}z4x%f %Bsource%b [-c|--compile] [--] [<file>]...

Source the specified Zsh files, skipping over inexisting ones.
If %B-c%b or %B--compile%b is specified, files are automatically compiled with
%F{2}zcompile%f to speed up subsequent sourcing, which boosts Zsh startup.

Relative file names are resolved from %U$ZDOTDIR/%u, e.g., the command below
sources %U$ZDOTIDIR/plugins/ohmyzsh/lib/diagnostics.zsh%u:

  %F{2}z4x%f %Bsource%b plugins/ohmyzsh/lib/diagnostics.zsh

Exit code of %F{2}z4x%f %Bsource%b is that of the last sourced file. Inexisting
files do not affect exit code.

Compilation isn't enabled by default because it has one negative side effect.
Namely, aliases defined within a sourced file are not expanded in that same
file. For example:

  %% %F{2}cat%f %U~/config.zsh%u

    %F{2}alias%f echo=%F{3}'echo hello'%f
    %F{2}echo%f world

  %% ( %F{2}z4x%f source %U~/config.zsh%u )

    hello world

  %% ( %F{2}z4x%f source -c %U~/config.zsh%u )

    world
END
)"

